-- test/fixtures/3.8.0-scene-calls.lua
-- The engine calls two format 10 scenes send as they are recalled and
-- played, for test/unit/system_38_test.lua ("a format 10 scene plays the
-- steps it played in 3.8.0" and "a format 10 scene with a gated voice, a
-- plain step and a lock plays as it did in 3.8.0"): the regression net of
-- the grid sequencer's Review Focus 1 (its plan's package 1a), which every
-- package of that plan keeps green. Each list is one run of SCENE.lines
-- there: test/fixtures/format-10-files.lua's scenes.data (for "gated", as
-- SCENE.gated_text edits it: voice 2's seq_gate 2, its step 1 at level 15
-- with nothing set, its step 9 at level 12 with a pitch lock of 1.5) in a
-- fresh data folder, math.randomseed(38) before the load, h.load_strata()
-- and h.finish_startup(context), the calls cleared, recall_scene(1), the
-- clocks run 1 s, the patterns started, run for 32 steps of 1/16 at 120
-- BPM (4 s less 10 ms) and stopped, with math.random replaced for the play
-- by a MINSTD generator seeded 38 (so the step's prob draws the same under
-- Lua 5.3 and LuaJIT). Every call from the recall on is here: the recall's
-- sets and its full sync of voices 1 and 2 (whose source and type it
-- changes), then the steps. The scenes: voice 1 on buffer 1, voice 2 on the
-- ring type with its step 3 at level 9, prob 40, notes {0, 7} and ratchet
-- 3, every voice saved in accent (but voice 2 in "gated"), LFO 1 on v2_main
-- (the setFastOffset lines).
--
-- How it was recorded (2026-11-24, fix round 1 of 1a, which added the
-- recall and the second scene): from an export of main at 71c03cec (`git
-- archive 71c03cec`, before package 1a changed anything) in a scratch
-- folder, by a throwaway unit file there (never committed) that loads the
-- SCENE table of the package's test/unit/system_38_test.lua (the same
-- steps, as text) and writes each line of SCENE.lines as h.call_line does
-- (`name(args)`, numbers "%.9g", strings "%q"); run with `lua test/run.lua
-- --dir <its folder>` from the export (Lua 5.3.6), the same file under
-- LuaJIT 2.1 and a second Lua run gave the same 909 lines. The name says
-- 3.8.0, though main at 71c03cec is not 3.8.0 in what every scene plays
-- (3.9's first part changed the steps after a direction change, #874, and
-- the missteps, #961 and #970; these scenes play forward with no misstep):
-- it is the baseline the grid sequencer's packages start from, so any
-- difference from it is one of theirs. The test compares through
-- h.canonical_call_lines on both sides, as the start fixtures' tests do,
-- and allows one difference: 1a's gateFloor 0 in each of the two syncs.
